# EAS Build archives from the repository root, not from mobile/ (confirmed via
# `eas build:inspect --stage archive`) — this monorepo's other packages (web-portal, backend)
# ride along in every mobile build's upload unless excluded here. IMPORTANT: once ANY
# .easignore exists, EAS CLI stops respecting every .gitignore in the tree entirely (they
# don't merge) — so this one file has to independently cover what each package's own
# .gitignore already does, not just add to it.
#
# What was actually inflating the archive (found via `eas build:inspect -p android -s archive
# -o <dir> -e preview`, du -sh on the result): NOT node_modules (already excluded by EAS's own
# default, archive-stage behavior) — it was web-portal/.next, a Next.js build cache that
# regrows from ordinary `next dev`/`next build` usage and reached 700+ MB. Its own
# web-portal/.gitignore already lists `/.next/`, but that's a package-rooted pattern
# (`/.next/` relative to web-portal/, not the git root) — the kind of nested-.gitignore rule
# EAS's own docs (expo.fyi/eas-build-archive) call out as unreliable once files are walked
# from the repo root, which is exactly what silently let it through.

# --- Node / Expo (mobile, web-portal) ---
node_modules/
.next/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- mobile: generated native folders (EAS's own prebuild regenerates these) ---
/mobile/ios
/mobile/android
.kotlin/

# --- Python (backend) ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- large study/analysis outputs (docs/10-project-structure.md §6) ---
artifacts/
*.parquet
*.npz

# --- secrets — EXPO_PUBLIC_* values come from EAS's own environment variables for mobile
# builds (see the build log's "Resolved ... environment" line), never a local .env file ---
.env*.local
.env*
!.env.example

# --- debug logs / OS / editor cruft ---
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem

# --- VCS / tooling, not part of any app ---
.git/
.claude/
.github/
